{
    "title": "Playful Eats: Fix Picky Eating",
    "description": "<h1><b>Help Your Picky Eater Learn to Like New Foods</b>\r\n\r\nPlayful Eats is designed to help children aged 0-8 improve eating habits and expand their diet, whether you have a new eater, a picky toddler, or an older child.</h1>\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>In-App Games, Books, Songs, and More</b>\r\n\r\nExpanding your child\u2019s diet starts <i>before</i> the food is in front of them at the table. Keep your child engaged in stress-free food learning through our kid-friendly, in-app activities. Try: Poke It, Food Puzzles, Interactive Food-Themed Books, or get a catchy Food Song stuck in your head.\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Learn from a Team of Pediatric Feeding Specialists</b>\r\n\r\nBased on the latest research, our team of speech, occupational therapy, and dietitian specialists have worked to create an achievable home program for you and your child.\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Answer All Your Food Concerns</b>\r\n\r\nIs my child eating enough? How can I keep them at the table longer? Can I get them to eat more veggies (and do they need them)? Our feeding experts have all the answers for you. Our parent-friendly, interactive learning modules can be completed at your own pace, and address multiple learning styles with videos, images, and real-life scenarios. \r\n\r\nFollow our guided Journey to gain knowledge on a wide range of topics, including: Staying at the Table, Veggies, Proteins, Magic Mealtime Words, Meal Timing, Reducing Mealtime Stress, and Sensory Components of Eating.\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Real-Life Food Activities</b>\r\n\r\nApply your learning with guided food activities to try daily with your child. Build carrot castles and broccoli forests, take your tomatoes swimming, and score apple goals. Making new foods fun puts your child on a stress-free path toward getting ready to taste these new foods.\r\n\r\nChoose target foods in our Food Library, then use our visual guides to progress through increasingly challenging activities to Observe, Engage, Touch, Taste, and eventually Eat new foods.\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Kid-Friendly Recipes</b>\r\n\r\nKeep your child involved in the kitchen with our kid-friendly, visual recipes. Playful Eats recipes give you \u201cgrownup steps\u201d for you to follow, and \u201ckid steps\u201d for your child to follow, all while making easy and fun foods your child will want to eat.\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Structured Eating Practice</b>\r\n\r\nWant to help your child learn to like new foods, but not quite sure where to start? Are strategies like feeding your child, running after them with a spoon, or bribing for bites getting old? With the Playful Eats 4 step system of Exchange, Expose, Explore, and Expand, you\u2019ll learn exactly where to go next to help your picky eater.\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Track Progress and Enhance Your Eating Experience</b>\r\n\r\nPlayful Eats includes tons of supplemental features to keep you and your child having fun with food. Check out our Food Tracker to watch your child\u2019s progress with target foods over time.  Use the Visual Scheduler to add structure to mealtimes, help your child understand mealtime expectations, and stay at the table longer. Check out your Toolbox for visuals and reminders to use at mealtimes and when problems arise. Explore our Sensory Play Bonus activities for additional fun preparation for eating more foods, just like in pediatric feeding therapy.\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Make Meals Easier and More Fun</b>\r\n\r\nWith your monthly subscription, you'll unlock everything Playful Eats has to get your child on the path to improved eating habits. Get started with your free trial to explore all the features at your fingertips.\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Download Now!</b>",
    "descriptionHTML": "<h1><b>Help Your Picky Eater Learn to Like New Foods</b><br><br>Playful Eats is designed to help children aged 0-8 improve eating habits and expand their diet, whether you have a new eater, a picky toddler, or an older child.</h1><br><br><br><b>In-App Games, Books, Songs, and More</b><br><br>Expanding your child\u2019s diet starts <i>before</i> the food is in front of them at the table. Keep your child engaged in stress-free food learning through our kid-friendly, in-app activities. Try: Poke It, Food Puzzles, Interactive Food-Themed Books, or get a catchy Food Song stuck in your head.<br><br><br><b>Learn from a Team of Pediatric Feeding Specialists</b><br><br>Based on the latest research, our team of speech, occupational therapy, and dietitian specialists have worked to create an achievable home program for you and your child.<br><br><br><b>Answer All Your Food Concerns</b><br><br>Is my child eating enough? How can I keep them at the table longer? Can I get them to eat more veggies (and do they need them)? Our feeding experts have all the answers for you. Our parent-friendly, interactive learning modules can be completed at your own pace, and address multiple learning styles with videos, images, and real-life scenarios. <br><br>Follow our guided Journey to gain knowledge on a wide range of topics, including: Staying at the Table, Veggies, Proteins, Magic Mealtime Words, Meal Timing, Reducing Mealtime Stress, and Sensory Components of Eating.<br><br><br><b>Real-Life Food Activities</b><br><br>Apply your learning with guided food activities to try daily with your child. Build carrot castles and broccoli forests, take your tomatoes swimming, and score apple goals. Making new foods fun puts your child on a stress-free path toward getting ready to taste these new foods.<br><br>Choose target foods in our Food Library, then use our visual guides to progress through increasingly challenging activities to Observe, Engage, Touch, Taste, and eventually Eat new foods.<br><br><br><b>Kid-Friendly Recipes</b><br><br>Keep your child involved in the kitchen with our kid-friendly, visual recipes. Playful Eats recipes give you \u201cgrownup steps\u201d for you to follow, and \u201ckid steps\u201d for your child to follow, all while making easy and fun foods your child will want to eat.<br><br><br><b>Structured Eating Practice</b><br><br>Want to help your child learn to like new foods, but not quite sure where to start? Are strategies like feeding your child, running after them with a spoon, or bribing for bites getting old? With the Playful Eats 4 step system of Exchange, Expose, Explore, and Expand, you\u2019ll learn exactly where to go next to help your picky eater.<br><br><br><b>Track Progress and Enhance Your Eating Experience</b><br><br>Playful Eats includes tons of supplemental features to keep you and your child having fun with food. Check out our Food Tracker to watch your child\u2019s progress with target foods over time.  Use the Visual Scheduler to add structure to mealtimes, help your child understand mealtime expectations, and stay at the table longer. Check out your Toolbox for visuals and reminders to use at mealtimes and when problems arise. Explore our Sensory Play Bonus activities for additional fun preparation for eating more foods, just like in pediatric feeding therapy.<br><br><br><b>Make Meals Easier and More Fun</b><br><br>With your monthly subscription, you&#39;ll unlock everything Playful Eats has to get your child on the path to improved eating habits. Get started with your free trial to explore all the features at your fingertips.<br><br><br><b>Download Now!</b>",
